      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:61:13",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الرَّجُلِ يَتَقَيَّأُ فِي ثَوْبِهِ يَجُوزُ أَنْ يُصَلِّيَ فِيهِ وَ لَا يَغْسِلَهُ قَالَ لَا بَأْسَ بِهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Idrees, from Muhammad Bin Ahmad, from Ahmad Bin Al Hassan Bin Ali, from Amro Bin Saeed, from Musaddiq Bin Sadaqa, from Ammar who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about the man who vomits in his clothes. Is it allowed for him that he prays <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span> in it and he has not washed it?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘There is no problem with it’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "13. Ahmad ibn Idris has narrated from Muhammad ibn Ahmad from Ahmad ibn al-Hassan ibn Ali from ‘Amr ibn Sa‘id from Musaddiq ibn Sadaqah from ‘Ammar who has said the following: “I once asked abu ’Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about a man who vomits in his clothes, if he can perform Salah (prayer) in them without washing. He (the Imam) said, ’It is not an offense to do so.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
